setup_prompt:
Help me connect Trillion to the AI app I use, so you (or that app) can use Trillion's tools. Set up only the AI app I am using or explicitly choose. If that AI cannot connect, or the required sign-in or connector is unavailable, stop at that exact boundary and tell me what is missing; never choose the first installed or shipped AI, CLI, model, or another app as a fallback. Trillion is an MCP server at this address: {mcp}
It signs in with OAuth and your Trillion sign-in. I never need a password or an API key for it. Also offer me the Trillion apps for my devices (step 1a), only from the links given there. If one is not out yet, say that plainly and never tell me to install an untrusted copy or load an unpacked folder.

Please do this:
1. If you can run terminal commands yourself, do the setup for me instead of explaining it:
{terminal_setup}
   Then offer the apps and configure this selected harness:
   a) {devices_step}
   b) {harness_setup}
2. Otherwise, ask me which app I want to connect, then walk me through its steps below ONE step at a time. For each step tell me the exact menu or button to click, what to type or paste, and what to leave alone. Wait for me to say done before giving the next step. Then tell me what I should see if it worked. On Trillion's sign-in page I can use my email and password, a passkey, or choose Email me a code.
{app_guides}
3. If what I see on my screen does not match your step, ask me to describe the screen and adjust. Never ask me for a password, an API key or a client id, never send me a 127.0.0.1 link, and never ask me to copy an address back to you.
4. When it is connected, list Trillion's tools to show it works. If you only walked me through connecting another app, give me the Trillion apps for my devices from step 1a too. Then ask me what I want to do first.
